# Dictionary for `patch`.
#
# Three formats behind three magics. `detect` dispatches on the first four or five bytes, so
# without these tokens two of the three decoders are unreachable.

"PATCH"
"EOF"
"UPS1"
"BPS1"

# IPS RLE marker: a zero-length record means "run-length", and the length that follows is the one
# that decides how much gets written.
"\x00\x00"
"\xff\xff\xff"

# Varint continuation bytes. UPS and BPS both use a variable-length integer whose shift must be
# checked *before* shifting — `1u64 << 70` is a debug panic and a release wrong-answer — so a long
# run of continuation bytes is precisely the input that matters.
"\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80\x80"
"\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff\x7f"
